* ============================================================
*  PINOCCHIO PARALLEL DIFFERENTIAL -- SET PARALLEL OFF vs ON (AIF-168 PERF-2)
*
*  Status:  CANDIDATE / REVIEW_BEFORE_EXECUTION. READ-ONLY.
*  Purpose: G-P2's own terms -- the same statements BOTH modes, identities
*           EXACT both modes, plus torn-partition probes whose bands straddle
*           the 6-worker partition boundaries. A wrong parallel answer must be
*           impossible to miss: every pair below must print IDENTICAL counts.
*
*  PARTITION ARITHMETIC (1M rows, 6 workers): base 166666 remainder 4, so
*  boundaries fall after recnos 166667, 333334, 500001, 666668, 833334.
*  SID == 50000000 + recno - 1, so bands of the form
*  [50000000+boundary-50, +50) tear across a partition seam.
*
*  DECLINE HONESTY: P1 probes a subquery predicate under PARALLEL ON and must
*  print "parallel declined -- subquery predicate" then the EXACT serial
*  answer. P2 probes the small-table decline on the 200-row x64 sample.
*
*  DEFERRED to the registered regression (owner-scoped): the DELETED-flag
*  probe needs a fixture with deleted rows per partition; the read-only
*  pinocchio fixtures carry none. Recorded, not waved.
*
*  RUNTIME: roughly 8-15 min post-PERF-1b (the OFF legs dominate).
* ============================================================
SET ECHO OFF
SET TIMER ON
SET TALK ON

SET PATH DBF DBF/pinocchio
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/pinocchio
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/pinocchio

ECHO === D0. open STUDENTS + ENROLL; assert PARALLEL starts OFF ===
SELECT 1
USE STUDENTS
SELECT 2
USE ENROLL
SELECT 1
SET PARALLEL STATUS

ECHO === D1-OFF. function-WHERE count (I5 form): expect 90700 ===
SET PARALLEL OFF
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE ALLTRIM(MAJOR) = 'CSCI'
ECHO === D1-ON. same statement, workers=6: expect 90700 and the workers=6 path line ===
SET PARALLEL 6
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE ALLTRIM(MAJOR) = 'CSCI'

ECHO === D2. torn-partition bands, OFF then ON -- five seams, expect 100 each, ALL pairs equal ===
SET PARALLEL OFF
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50166617 AND SID < 50166717
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50333284 AND SID < 50333384
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50499951 AND SID < 50500051
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50666618 AND SID < 50666718
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50833284 AND SID < 50833384
SET PARALLEL 6
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50166617 AND SID < 50166717
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50333284 AND SID < 50333384
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50499951 AND SID < 50500051
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50666618 AND SID < 50666718
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50833284 AND SID < 50833384

ECHO === D3. bare COUNT(*) both modes: expect 1000000 twice ===
SET PARALLEL OFF
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS
SET PARALLEL 6
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS

ECHO === D4. row-returning + ORDER BY + LIMIT both modes: SAME 5 rows, same order ===
SET PARALLEL OFF
SQLSEL SELECT SID,LNAME FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID < 50000100 ORDER BY LNAME LIMIT 5
SET PARALLEL 6
SQLSEL SELECT SID,LNAME FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID < 50000100 ORDER BY LNAME LIMIT 5

ECHO === D5. ENROLL at 5.5M both modes over the seek-join fact: expect 5501358 ===
SELECT 2
SET PARALLEL OFF
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ENROLL
SET PARALLEL 6
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ENROLL
SELECT 1

ECHO === P1. DECLINE HONESTY: subquery predicate under ON must decline + exact 1000 ===
SET PARALLEL 6
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS S WHERE S.SID IN (SELECT E.SID FROM ENROLL E WHERE E.SID < 50001000)

ECHO === P2. DECLINE HONESTY: 11-row MAJORS must decline (too small) + exact 11 ===
* (First-run lesson 2026-09-22: the original probe opened the 200-row x64
*  sample as STUDENTS while pinocchio STUDENTS was open in area 1, and the
*  by-name resolver correctly picked the FIRST open match -- the probe
*  measured the wrong table. MAJORS is unique by name and 11 rows.)
SELECT 3
USE MAJORS
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM MAJORS
CLOSE
SELECT 1

ECHO === D6. cleanup: PARALLEL back OFF (the default this build ships with) ===
SET PARALLEL OFF
SET PARALLEL STATUS
SELECT 2
CLOSE
SELECT 1
CLOSE

ECHO ============================================================
ECHO PARALLEL DIFFERENTIAL COMPLETE. Confirm and record:
ECHO   D1 : 90700 == 90700; the ON leg prints workers=6 in its path line.
ECHO   D2 : five torn-seam bands, 100 each, OFF == ON pairwise.
ECHO   D3 : 1000000 == 1000000.   D5: 5501358 == 5501358.
ECHO   D4 : identical 5 rows in identical order (ORDER BY sorts the merge).
ECHO   P1 : declined (subquery; INNER select parallelizes) + 1000 exact.
ECHO   P2 : declined (too small) + 11 exact.
ECHO   ELAPSED ratios OFF vs ON are the speedup datum; record the curve by
ECHO   rerunning D1/D3 at SET PARALLEL 2, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 22 (OQ-P1).
ECHO ============================================================
